WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.072 --> 00:00:03.822
(dramatic music)

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.131
- In "Top Boy," black men
live with heavy pressures.

00:00:09.131 --> 00:00:11.881
(dramatic music)

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.660
Many of the men in the series
are sweeping up the pieces

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.350
of shattered families,
feeling their way through life

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.333
in the city's most deprived estates.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.170
- I'm Aniefiok Ekpoudom,
a freelance writer

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.850
and storyteller from South London.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.010
And today, I'm gonna talk to you

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.843
about some of the men in Top Boy.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.290
- You need to be there for her you know.

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:42.691
- What?

00:00:42.691 --> 00:00:45.400
- Dads, to be there for
their daughters, man.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.350
- Top Boy is full of tired
men eager and anxious

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:51.250
about providing for and
protecting their young children.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:52.810
Among the high drama of their lives

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.820
where they risk freedom for quick wins,

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:57.430
they're haunted by the fear
that their efforts aren't enough

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:59.330
that the money they
bring in is not enough.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:01.429
That, as men, they are not enough.

00:01:01.429 --> 00:01:03.470
- That right there is my little girl.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:07.930
When her daddy comes home,
that little girl needs

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.780
to be standing in front of a hero,

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.810
not a fuckin' con in prison stink.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:18.830
- [Aniefiok] Sully is no
different, because he was in jail

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:20.660
he was absent when his daughter grew up.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.100
And is now weighed by a pressure

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.363
to present himself as
a hero upon his return.

00:01:25.472 --> 00:01:29.797
- That's all I am right
now, a fuckin' broke con.

00:01:29.797 --> 00:01:31.950
- [Aniefiok] "Top Boy"
sees black men hunting down

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.840
goalposts that are forever shifting.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.423
- That's why we come here
i'nt it, on their birthdays?

00:01:36.423 --> 00:01:39.010
- Happy birthday mum.
- Happy birthday mum.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.700
- [Aniefiok] When their
mother died of cancer

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.830
and their father tragically
passed soon after,

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:45.250
Jamie and his two brothers
where left orphaned.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:46.910
The responsibility fell on the eldest

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:48.475
to step up for his siblings.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:50.620
- Who better at cooking, me
or Aaron, it's me isn't it?

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:52.333
- Pound one, you know how to cook.

00:01:52.333 --> 00:01:53.840
- Hey yo, don't be lyin' to the kid fam,

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.195
you know he's not in my league.

00:01:55.195 --> 00:01:56.350
- Shut up, man

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.210
- The youngest brother, Steph,

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:00.130
now looks to Jamie as a safety blanket.

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:04.863
- Hey Jamie, can you wake
me up when you come in?

00:02:04.863 --> 00:02:06.690
I can't go sleep unless you come in.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:10.070
- Regardless of whether Jamie
feels ready, or feels capable

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:11.490
he has little choice but to provide

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.660
for his siblings in whatever way possible.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:14.493
- Next time I'm here I wanna hear

00:02:14.493 --> 00:02:16.150
you're doin' as well as Ax, yeah?

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.520
- He turns to the opportunities
he sees in his environment.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.430
- I'm wearin' the fuckin' force, cous'.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.780
- Nah, you aint.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.170
- [Aniefiok] In trying to do
so, "Top Boy" gives context

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.810
to why some young men might risk

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.650
their freedom and lives on the roads.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.720
Perhaps the most tragic example is Ax.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.940
A home visit from
immigration officers leaves

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.990
his mum's citizenship in jeopardy.

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:38.406
- She's really sad,
man, like all the time.

00:02:38.406 --> 00:02:39.593
I don't know what to do.

00:02:39.593 --> 00:02:40.960
- [Aniefiok] Over the
course of the season,

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.760
we watch him fall into
a state of desperation.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.370
He tries to fix their money troubles,

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:47.470
first, by sellin' burgers
outside of school.

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:49.500
Then, attempting to steal and sell dogs.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.809
And, eventually as a last resort, beggin'

00:02:51.809 --> 00:02:54.710
the Summerhouse crew for an
introduction into drug dealin'.

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:55.850
- I don't have a phone.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:58.940
- Shit well no wonder you want
to start shuttin' your mouth.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:01.070
- At the end of the
season, the high achieving,

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:04.220
happy student is gone,
replaced by a young man

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:06.300
who will do anything he
can to piece together

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.130
a home that is slowly fallin' apart.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.790
The strains of providing
inevitably leave cracks

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.820
and throughout the season
we see this portrayed

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.330
through Jamie and Aaron's
complex relationship.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.160
- You ain't my dad bruv.
- Yes, I am.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:17.993
- No, you're not.

00:03:17.993 --> 00:03:19.750
- See me here, I'm your father, yeah?

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.247
I'm your mother, I'm your older brother.

00:03:21.247 --> 00:03:23.090
- "Top Boy" shows these are the frictions

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.160
that arise when a son is
turned parent too soon.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:27.210
When a boy becomes a man too early.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:28.870
When the innocence of
youth is stripped away

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.640
without warning, and he's left alone

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.793
to stare down the anxieties of adulthood.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:36.093
- Brothers go, right?
- Yeah, man.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.220
- There was no rubric left for Jamie

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.780
that taught him what it
means to be a father.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.040
He's learnin' as he goes, feeling his way

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:45.330
through the world with no
guidance and no role model.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.140
The only signpost of parenthood he has

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:50.310
are the striking traits he
remembers in his parents.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:52.130
The resilience he recalls in his mum,

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:54.780
and the authoritative tone
that radiated from his dad.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:57.623
Both are attributes he
feels he now must embody.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.280
- So proud of you, bruv (kissing sound).

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.774
Meanwhile, Dushane is
chasing shadows of his own.

00:04:05.774 --> 00:04:07.333
- I'm 36 years old ...

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:12.741
I aint got no woman, no kids,

00:04:12.741 --> 00:04:15.780
fuckin' sleepin' on Dris' stinkin' sofa.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.350
- [Aniefiok] Tortured by his past glories

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:19.700
and perceived triumphs,
Dushane's obsession

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:21.170
with reachin' the top is one that,

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.830
eventually, corrupts his character

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:25.430
and adds a bleak
ruthlessness to his nature.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:29.093
- We fuckin' won ... what does it matter?

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:33.890
I did what I had to do
to get us back on top

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.900
and that's what a fuckin' leader does.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:36.910
- But at what cost?

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:40.540
By the end of the season he
loses almost all that he loves.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.170
His cousin rests in a
grave, his mum refuses

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.640
to see his face, and
he's wrecked the trust

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.890
of his only remaining friend.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:52.890
- Just because we didn't
lose, doesn't mean we won.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:55.580
- They're all collateral damage
of Dushane's frustration.

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:57.210
The harsh reality that he's a man

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:00.150
who's reached 36 years old
with little to show for it.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.050
But these characters
are not defined solely

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:04.337
by their quite fears of
appearing less than men.

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:06.790
"Top Boy" also finds
space for powerful moments

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:08.858
of intimacy and release.

00:05:08.858 --> 00:05:09.871
- So your man was in jail wasn't that

00:05:09.871 --> 00:05:13.260
when you was showin' me,
and I respect for that.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.470
- I've got you bro just like how

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:17.360
you've always had me, bruv.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.450
- These spaces are both
literal and symbolic.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:22.210
Sully finds solace in Jason,
opening up to his friend

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:24.640
when they briefly leave the
chaos of East London behind

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:27.053
and arrive in an English seaside town.

00:05:28.046 --> 00:05:30.323
- Well, you know, I ain't
never even seen the sea before.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:35.036
I never left the fucking country. (scoffs)

00:05:35.036 --> 00:05:39.170
I'm 35 years old and I never
left the country, imagine that.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:42.240
- With Jason, Sully unburdens
and feels secure enough

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:45.470
to lay himself bare, the town
gives a sense of isolation,

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:48.580
a reprieve from the relentless
nature of the big city.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:51.510
And, at times, while down in Ramsgate

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.400
the mask he wears for his
daughter briefly disappears

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:56.170
and it's as if he's fallen back in time.

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:57.740
He becomes just a kid messin' around

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.132
with mates on the beach.

00:05:59.132 --> 00:06:00.542
(firecracker sizzling and then going off).

00:06:00.542 --> 00:06:02.983
- (laughs) I swear I'm not
one of those fuckers, eh.

00:06:02.983 --> 00:06:06.409
Who gave that to you? (running on gravel)

00:06:06.409 --> 00:06:10.495
You fuckin' idiot (laughing),
you're full of shit.

00:06:10.495 --> 00:06:12.420
All right, all right it's cool.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:14.160
- [Aniefiok] It's a long deep exhale

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.720
for one of Top Boy's most
tormented individuals.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:18.230
One that reframes his character,

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:21.130
sheds free the fears that
surround emotional intimacy

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:23.460
and instead displays a sense of freedom

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:26.010
that emerges when space is
found for vulnerability.

00:06:27.077 --> 00:06:28.753
- Look, if you could have anything, yeah,

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.073
what would it be?

00:06:31.073 --> 00:06:33.219
- You know what, to go watch Arsenal play

00:06:33.219 --> 00:06:35.150
'cause they're the best fuckin' team

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:36.880
in the whole Premiere League.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.170
- In a similar fashion,
Kit is a release valve

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.813
and a gentle letdown
at Jamie's lowest hour.

00:06:46.563 --> 00:06:48.730
(sobbing)

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.050
It's a powerful scene that captures

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.690
a moment documented
rarely in British media,

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:58.470
that of two black men
curled in each other's arms.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:00.510
In "Top Boy" it served as a message

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:02.490
that although Jamie shoulders burdens

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:04.430
in the midst of turmoil he doesn't need

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:07.290
to face the world alone,
or with a brave face.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.180
Then, in the closing scenes of the season

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:11.952
Jamie's relationship with Aaron
boils to press this point.

00:07:11.952 --> 00:07:16.952
- This is your fault, bruv,
this is all your fault.

00:07:17.365 --> 00:07:21.963
You promised them, man, you promised them.

00:07:21.963 --> 00:07:24.600
You promised mum and dad you
were gonna take care of us.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:27.040
- [Aniefiok] And when it does,
the hard paternal exterior,

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:30.450
finally, melts away, their
father and son relationship

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:34.109
slowly ebbs out and the
siblings embrace in tears.

00:07:34.109 --> 00:07:34.942
- [Aaron] Fuckin' move.

00:07:34.942 --> 00:07:36.540
- [Jamie] Just chill, just chill.

00:07:39.066 --> 00:07:41.233
(sobbing)

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:47.680
- In their darkest hour they find comfort

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:50.060
and purge in each other's arms.

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:51.510
It's a bittersweet new beginning

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:54.080
for a difficult brotherhood,
and a revealing peek

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.270
into what occurs when boys
are unknowingly thrust

00:07:56.270 --> 00:07:58.200
into the role of providers.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.000
In all, "Top Boy" is a glimpse

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.930
into the crises that can fray and mend

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:03.480
the relationships between men

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.780
and those who they love most dearly.

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:08.640
It's a vivid depiction,
and an intense exploration

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.870
of the pressures of male adulthood

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:12.453
in black Britain and beyond.

00:08:13.321 --> 00:08:16.404
(gentle piano music)

